    "background_story": "Elsa was a brilliant and eccentric art historian, specializing in the works of William Hogarth, a renowned 18th-century English artist. Her fascination with Hogarth's satirical engravings and paintings led her to write a groundbreaking thesis that shed new light on his artistic intentions. Elsa's research took her to the streets of London, where she meticulously recreated Hogarth's iconic scenes, from 'Marriage \u00e0-la-mode' to 'Gin Lane'. Her passion project, a Hogarth-inspired graphic novel, earned her critical acclaim and a coveted spot in a prestigious art museum. Elsa's love for Hogarth's art had not only deepened her understanding of the past but also inspired her to create something innovative and thought-provoking, leaving a lasting impact on the art world.",
